--TEST--
a class of the program that extends a type may not declare a name an `extend` block adds to that type, so a call never reaches a different member through a different static type: the added member is `E1011`, and the error shows the subclass's method — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Acme\Shop\Order;

autoload 'Acme\Shop' from './vendor/acme/shop/src';

extend Order as OrderTools {
    public function isLarge(): bool {
        return $this->total > 100;
    }
}

final class BigOrder extends Order
{
    public function isLarge(): bool
    {
        return true;
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--FILE vendor/acme/shop/src/Order.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Acme\Shop;

class Order
{
    public function constructor(public int $total) {}
}
--FILE vendor/acme/shop/package.toml--
[package]
name = 'Acme\Shop'
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1011]: `App\BigOrder` extends `Acme\Shop\Order` and declares a method named `isLarge`
   --> %s:9:21
   |
 9 |     public function isLarge(): bool {
   |                     ^^^^^^^ this name is already used
...
16 |     public function isLarge(): bool
   |                     ------- `App\BigOrder::isLarge` is declared here
   = help: give the added member a different name. An added member never replaces or overrides another member

error: aborting due to 1 error
%A
